The '''Shansi national football team''' ({{Lang-yue|山西足球代表隊}}) represents [[Shansi]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Shansi Football Association]] and competes as a member of the East Fosian Football Federation within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Shansi are currently ranked 28th in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their fourth [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Early years ===
Shansi's football development accelerated after the formation of the Shansi Premier League in 1985. The league's physical, high-tempo style produced players who excelled in East Fosian competitions and attracted attention from clubs in Okaiken and Nakamizu.

=== World Cup history ===
Shansi first qualified for the World Cup in 2006, followed by appearances in 2010 and 2014. The 2014 tournament saw Shansi reach the round of 16, their best result to date, before elimination by a strong Mesogean side. The 2022 qualification marks a return to the tournament after missing 2018.

